{
  "$comment": "BYOK image task management. Pure logic shared by iOS / Android / Web; scripts/studio-contracts-check.mjs recomputes every case with scripts/lib/studio-image-reference.mjs. Inputs are already-typed values (profile fields were validated by profile resolution, n and batches by param normalization), so nothing here is decoded from the wire. Test groups, same name on every end: spec, timeout, retry, transportPhase, aggregate, queue, reconcile.",
  "contractId": "byok_image_tasks.v1",
  "version": 1,
  "spec": {
    "defaultTimeoutSeconds": 180,
    "maxTimeoutSeconds": 180,
    "maxConcurrentRounds": 4,
    "maxAutoRetries": 1,
    "phases": [
      "pre_connect",
      "after_send",
      "timeout",
      "cancelled"
    ],
    "reconcileActions": [
      "keep",
      "process",
      "keep_running",
      "interrupted",
      "failed_timeout"
    ],
    "roundStatuses": [
      "completed",
      "partial",
      "failed",
      "cancelled"
    ],
    "rules": [
      "timeout: per HTTP attempt total duration = profile.timeoutSeconds; missing (null) or <= 0 -> 180; capped at 180. A retry gets a fresh full timeout.",
      "retry: only a pre_connect failure (DNS, refused, no route, TLS handshake / certificate, offline) on the first attempt (attempt 0) is retried, once. after_send, timeout and cancelled are never retried; HTTP responses never reach this function (error classification decides). Output errorKind uses image_error_samples.v1.json kinds; mayBeBilled is true once the body may have reached the provider (after_send, timeout).",
      "transportPhase: per-end mapping of platform transport errors to a phase; checks run in the listed order and anything unknown is after_send (no retry). Only a signal that proves the body was not sent is pre_connect: a timeout an end cannot place before the body (iOS -1001, Android SocketTimeoutException incl. OkHttp connect timeout) is timeout, while Web undici UND_ERR_CONNECT_TIMEOUT is pre_connect. Wrapped errors: check the error itself, then its cause chain outer-first; the first layer that matches wins (Android cause, Web cause.cause...).",
      "aggregate: only results[0 ..< batches.length] count (extra results are ignored, missing ones count as 0 images without errorKind); each batch's images are capped at that batch size (negative -> 0), then summed. delivered >= n -> completed; 0 < delivered < n -> partial; 0 -> failed. errorKind = first non-null batch errorKind by batch index; if none, partial -> 'partial', failed -> 'decode_failed'. cancelled wins and drops everything (delivered 0).",
      "queue: one slot per round (a multi-model comparison is one round per model); all batches of a round run inside its slot. FIFO. submit of an id already running or queued is a no-op. cancel of a running round frees the slot immediately (mayBeBilled true) and promotes the queue head; cancel of a queued round never sends a request (mayBeBilled false); cancel / finish of an unknown id is a no-op. response for a running id -> accept, otherwise drop (late reply after cancel is never persisted). Effects are listed in emission order.",
      "reconcile: on launch, terminal statuses -> keep; queued -> interrupted (never sent, not re-queued); running: responseReceived -> process; transferActive -> keep_running; no startedAtMs or clock went backwards (nowMs < startedAtMs) -> interrupted; nowMs - startedAtMs >= effective timeout * 1000 -> failed_timeout; otherwise interrupted."
    ]
  },
  "timeout": [
    {
      "caseId": "timeout.missing",
      "timeoutSeconds": null,
      "expect": 180
    },
    {
      "caseId": "timeout.zero",
      "timeoutSeconds": 0,
      "expect": 180
    },
    {
      "caseId": "timeout.negative",
      "timeoutSeconds": -5,
      "expect": 180
    },
    {
      "caseId": "timeout.one",
      "timeoutSeconds": 1,
      "expect": 1
    },
    {
      "caseId": "timeout.short",
      "timeoutSeconds": 60,
      "expect": 60
    },
    {
      "caseId": "timeout.at_cap",
      "timeoutSeconds": 180,
      "expect": 180
    },
    {
      "caseId": "timeout.over_cap",
      "timeoutSeconds": 181,
      "expect": 180
    },
    {
      "caseId": "timeout.managed_value_capped",
      "timeoutSeconds": 240,
      "expect": 180
    }
  ],
